--TEST--
`Ad::memberOf` takes the group's DN, which the server reads as a path in the tree, so a `tainted` string does not compile there, and a DN the program wrote does — ADR 0278 § 1 and `rule:core-classes/ldap-dn-is-the-launderer`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Groups {
    public static function members(tainted string $group): void {
        var $written = Core\Ldap\Ad::memberOf("CN=Staff,DC=example,DC=test");
        var $typed = Core\Ldap\Ad::memberOf($group, {nested: true});
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string|Core\Ldap\Dn`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:5:45
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
